bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_build_hir_sigsegv_under_20g_cgroup_cuda_port_closure_2026-11-22, 0, "2026-11-22 filed by work/cuda-compiler-bugs: stage2 ef46f0d2 port_owner native-build SIGSEGV (worker -139, rc 117) at HIR 82/514 under MemoryMax=20G in 3 configs, peak RSS 4.01 GB; 8G control passes. HIR order diverges after lib.nogc_sync_mut.io.process_ops. Crash file /var/crash/_home_yoon_dev_simple-integ5-20261116_build_bootstrap_pinned-src_pinned-c1a10190b978_build_bootstrap-s2probe-integ25_stage3_aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu_stage2-admitted_simple.1000.crash."
    native_build_hir_sigsegv_under_20g_cgroup_cuda_port_closure_2026-11-22, 1, "2026-11-26 ROOT CAUSE (lane work/bug-cuda-segv-20261126, fix 22fb17305f0 + 794d8c100d7): not the cgroup. 20G only admits 3 parse shards that warm the frontend cache; 8G + copied warm frontend cache + SIMPLE_HIR_CACHE=0 SIGSEGVs at the same HIR 82/514. gdb watchpoint: paused-born join_point_attr_dirty_fn_names header freed by free_transient_objects at module 81 scope end (Rust runtime). Only rt_array_free untracked freed objects from the transient scope; rt_string_free and other unregister_heap_ptr* frees left stale entries whose address was reused by paused allocations (10/12 observed reuses came from rt_string_free). Fix: untrack on every registry erase; Rust unit test red->green; runtime lib 1572/1572. C twin not affected: array/dict/enum/closure/scalar reclaim compares per-object transient_scope_id; paused-born strings carry no TRANSIENT flag or TRANSIENT|SESSION, both skipped at scope end. Fix implemented at 794d8c100d7, unpushed. Verification pending: stage2 producer embeds the frozen runtime; needs the next Stage 2 build to rerun the 8G warm-cache recipe."

